KZ3 patch 2083: review fixes for 2078-2082 (pass 77).

- NV3089 source origin: IMAGE_IN_POINT is u (low 16) / v (high 16) in 12.4 and ds_dx/dt_dy are 12.20, but the
  guest-memory copies (swizzled and linear) and 2080's row copy added u << 8 (a 12.12 value), reading column u >> 12;
  the GPU mirror uses (u & 0xFFFF) >> 4. Now u << 16 (row copy: u >> 4). Blits with a source origin >= 16 px wrote
  the wrong pixels into guest memory. Upstream candidate (cellGcmSys.c nv3089_blit).
- Location 1 (IO-mapped main memory), where the clean-page hash skip is on by default (2080): PPU stores there noted
  nothing. The walker now NOTE-marks the EA pages behind each location-1 span it would skip
  (cellGcm_ppu_note_io_span; ppu_store_note_pages returns the pages it changed, and a span with a fresh page hashes
  once), the PPU store hook notes IO-mapped EAs as location 1, and an unmap clears the bits.
- LD_TEX_WRITER diagnostic: one packed u64 per page (frame, mark sequence, source) written in one store, and the
  verdict compares the mark sequence with the entry's sequence before its last hash (rsx_tex_writer.h), so a tracked
  write in the hash's own frame is no longer reported as an untracked writer.

Host tests: tools/smoke/test_nv3089_rows.sh (origin check vs the IMAGE_IN_POINT definition), test_tex_writer.sh.
Refreshed for v0.15.0 (SPU pass 85): upstream's new nv3089_engine_read (draw engine source read-back) had the same
12.12 end point (u << 8), so for u0 >= 16 px sx1 < sx0 and the read-back was skipped; it now uses << 16 as well.
